WEBVTT

00:00.258 --> 00:01.384
- [Voiceover] We're told the graph of y

00:01.384 --> 00:04.008
equals two to the x is
shown below, alright.

00:04.008 --> 00:05.377
Which of the following is the graph

00:05.377 --> 00:09.358
of y equals two to the
negative x minus five?

00:09.358 --> 00:10.577
So there's two changes here.

00:10.577 --> 00:13.271
Instead of two to the x, we
have two to the negative x

00:13.271 --> 00:14.431
and then, we're not leaving that alone,

00:14.431 --> 00:15.906
we, then, subtract five.

00:15.906 --> 00:17.636
So let's take 'em step by step.

00:17.636 --> 00:19.911
So let's first think about what y

00:19.911 --> 00:22.929
equals two to the negative
x would look like.

00:22.929 --> 00:25.670
Well, any input we now put into an x,

00:25.670 --> 00:27.306
we're now going to take the negative of.

00:27.306 --> 00:31.091
So if I input a two, it's
like taking the opposite

00:31.091 --> 00:35.572
of the two and then, inputting
that into two to the x.

00:35.572 --> 00:37.339
And so, what we're essentially going to do

00:37.339 --> 00:41.506
is flip this graph over the y-axis.

00:41.506 --> 00:44.885
So, here we have the point two comma four.

00:44.885 --> 00:46.544
Over here, we're going to have the point

00:46.544 --> 00:49.620
negative two comma four.

00:49.620 --> 00:52.303
When x is zero, they're going
to give us the same value.

00:52.303 --> 00:54.555
So they're both going to
have the same y-intercept.

00:54.555 --> 00:57.263
And so are graph is going to look like,

00:57.263 --> 01:01.327
our graph is going to
look something like, this.

01:01.327 --> 01:02.406
They're going to be mirror images

01:02.406 --> 01:04.820
flipped around the y-axis.

01:04.820 --> 01:09.820
So, it's going to look like that.

01:10.440 --> 01:15.440
That is the graph of y is
equal to two to the negative x.

01:15.687 --> 01:16.886
And then we have to worry about

01:16.886 --> 01:19.127
the subtracting five from it.

01:19.127 --> 01:20.868
Well, that's, you're subtracting five

01:20.868 --> 01:23.097
from your final y-value
so that's going to work.

01:23.097 --> 01:25.779
You're subtracting five
to get your y-value now,

01:25.779 --> 01:27.578
where your y-value is
going to be five lower,

01:27.578 --> 01:28.867
is I guess the best way to say it,

01:28.867 --> 01:31.699
so this is going to shift
the graph down by five.

01:31.699 --> 01:33.267
So instead of having
the y-intercept there,

01:33.267 --> 01:34.561
it's going to be five lower.

01:34.561 --> 01:38.908
One, two, one, each hash mark is two

01:38.908 --> 01:41.961
so this is one, two, three, four, five,

01:41.961 --> 01:43.319
is going to be right over there.

01:43.319 --> 01:47.417
So shift down by five, two, four, five.

01:47.417 --> 01:48.381
It's going to look like that.

01:48.381 --> 01:50.343
And the asymptote,
instead of the asymptote,

01:50.343 --> 01:54.243
going towards y equals zero, the asymptote

01:54.243 --> 01:58.341
is going to be at y is
equal to negative five.

01:58.341 --> 02:02.497
So the asymptote is going to
be y equals negative five.

02:02.497 --> 02:07.497
So it should look something like,

02:08.362 --> 02:13.214
something like what I
am drawing right now.

02:13.214 --> 02:17.324
Something like, something like that.

02:17.324 --> 02:18.984
So now we can look at which choices.

02:18.984 --> 02:21.457
So this should be the graph of y

02:21.457 --> 02:24.579
equals two to the negative x minus five.

02:24.579 --> 02:27.122
So let's see which of
these choices depict that.

02:28.267 --> 02:31.588
So this first choice
actually seems to be spot-on.

02:31.588 --> 02:33.364
It's exactly what we drew.

02:33.364 --> 02:35.697
Well, we can look at the
other ones, just in case.

02:35.697 --> 02:39.006
Well, this is, this looks like,
what did they do over here?

02:39.006 --> 02:40.863
Looks like they, instead of flipping over

02:40.863 --> 02:44.717
the y-axis, they took the,
they flipped over the x-axis

02:44.717 --> 02:47.004
and then they shifted
down, so that's not right.

02:47.004 --> 02:48.316
Here it looks like they got what we got

02:48.316 --> 02:50.835
but they flipped it over the x-axis.

02:50.835 --> 02:53.296
And this looks like they
flipped it over the y-axis

02:53.296 --> 02:54.922
but then they shifted,
instead of shifting down

02:54.922 --> 02:57.301
by five, it looks like they
